name o3-05-umbrella-held-1
timeout 600
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 5 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE FRIENDLY UMBRELLA, WEAPONS HOLD. CONTROL: o3-04-umbrella.fbm. ONE TOKEN CHANGES - the net's
# `wcs free` -> `wcs hold`. Same striker, same spawn, same store, same three batteries at the same
# coordinates with the same magazines and the same `emcon free`, same clock, same zones, same everything
# else. Callsigns are y5* rather than y4* because a controlled variant must not share a callsign with
# its control (the store carry is keyed by callsign) - O4's first rule.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# WHY THIS IS ITS OWN SORTIE AND NOT A REMARK. O2's rule 11: when a result says "this moves nothing",
# ask under which POLICY it was measured. o3-04 measured a friendly umbrella that spends its whole
# magazine on its own striker; that is the answer for `wcs free` and for nothing else.
# doc/air-defence-network.md §5 carries `free` / `tight` / `hold` as poles and expressly REFUSES to rank
# them. O3 therefore flies both, and this file is the half that a real air defence would actually have
# briefed on the afternoon of 6 October: THE MISSILES ARE HELD WHILE OUR OWN AIRCRAFT ARE INSIDE THE
# BOX. It is the only countermeasure to a missing IFF interrogator that this format can express, and it
# is a DECISION with a price rather than a fix.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file): the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 /
# Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21 of 6 October 1973, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may not answer a
# campaign question. It makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history. A bad O3 result therefore
# says more than the record did; a good one says nothing. The umbrella is NOT substituted - `sa2` /
# `sa3` / `sa6` are the anchor's own designations - but there are three batteries here against the
# anchor's >200, so every count is per-battery and never a theatre figure.
#
# WHAT `wcs hold` IS, mechanically, and what it is NOT. It is the fire-control AUTHORITY the NODE
# transmits over the net (doc/air-defence-network.md §5, §8), received by each member as a state it must
# obey. It does NOT switch a radar off: the batteries still radiate (`emcon free`), still take the
# node's cue, still find and still hold a firm track. The one thing they may not do is launch. So this
# file measures the cost of the DECISION and never the cost of going dark - o3-04's sibling in that
# other direction does not exist in this campaign, and W3/W4 have already measured emission discipline
# on both sides of its threshold.
#
# THE ARENA is o3-04's, unchanged, and its two derived facts are worth repeating because they still
# hold: the S-75's 450 m altitude FLOOR [T4] means it cannot engage a 300 m striker on either side, and
# the 300 m the KOLS rangefinder forces on the striker (o3-01's header) is exactly the band the S-125's
# 100 m and the 2K12's 50 m floors cover. Scale: 1 deg lat = 111 132 m, 1 deg lon at 30.80 N =
# 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES PUTTING THE UMBRELLA ON WEAPONS HOLD BUY, AND WHAT DOES IT COST?
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const), read against o3-04 line by line:
#   `site LAUNCH`                7 -> 0.        `site DEPLETED`   2 -> 0.
#   magazines at the end         0 + 0 -> 4 V-601 + 3 3M9 INTACT.
#   `net WCS ... state=hold ... effect="launch inhibited"`   0 -> 2 lines, one per battery at the tick
#                                its own reaction time elapsed on a correlated firm track (y5sa3 at
#                                t = 36.8 rangeM 32 221.5; y5sa6 at t = 130.9 rangeM 17 509.2). The
#                                inhibition is LOGGED where it bites, so the belt's restraint is an
#                                observable and not an absence - which is W5's rule 16 satisfied in
#                                advance: this is the RESTRAINED nothing, not the ABSENT one.
#   `site TRACK` / `site RADIATE` / `net CUE`   UNCHANGED - the batteries see exactly what they saw
#                                (`site TRACK unit=y5sa3` at t = 6.8, brgDeg 100.037, rangeM 25 583.8,
#                                identical to o3-04's).
#   the strike                   UNCHANGED to the centimetre: `aimErrM 66.39` (long -45.52, across
#                                +48.34), y5art DESTROYED at t = 26.2, the identical tick as o3-01 and
#                                o3-04.
#   aircraft lost                0 -> 0.
#   -> ON THIS GEOMETRY WEAPONS HOLD COSTS NOTHING AND BUYS THE MAGAZINE. Seven rounds that o3-04 threw
#      at its own striker are still on their rails at t = 600.
#   -> AND THAT IS ONLY HALF AN ANSWER, WHICH IS WHY IT IS SAID HERE AND NOT IN A SUMMARY: o3-04's seven
#      rounds killed nobody either, because a FlightBox belt cannot reach a 300 m target at all (the
#      ladder is in doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md §State). So the MEASURED difference between the
#      two policies is EXPENDITURE, not survival, and the survival half of the comparison is blocked by
#      a defect that this campaign found and did not fix. A reader who takes "hold costs nothing" as
#      doctrine is reading past that.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 = SUCCESS is the expected shape - every objective in the file is met, including
# all four `survive` lines on the ground, and the run goes to its 600 s timeout because the deferred
# objectives cannot conclude earlier. THE MEASUREMENT is the ABSENCE of `site LAUNCH` beside the
# PRESENCE of `net WCS ... effect="launch inhibited"`, read against o3-04's seven launches; then
# `stores DELIVERY` against o3-04's, which must be identical. exit 1 or 2 would be a defect.

zone umbrella 30.84000 32.31000 35000 100 18000
zone ceiling  30.80000 32.45000 60000 2200 20000

net crossing
  control y5nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs hold                               # THE ONE CHANGED TOKEN: o3-04 transmits `free`
  member y5nod
  member y5sa2
  member y5sa3
  member y5sa6

unit y5str
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.80000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.30000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y5art
  objective survive
  objective avoid zone ceiling

unit y5art
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.80000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

unit y5nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.26000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  objective survive

unit y5sa2
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 30.76000 32.28000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 6
  objective survive

unit y5sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 30.84000 32.31000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 4
  objective survive

unit y5sa6
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.40000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 3
  objective survive
